# HC32F460 boot/connect smoke test. HDSC has no upstream Renode
# CPU model and no upstream peripheral models for any of its blocks
# - the chip is end-to-end reachable only through the local
# hc32f460.repl plus the C# HC32F460_USART model
# (test/emulator/repl/hc32f460_uart.cs, Roslyn-compiled into the
# runtime via `i @file.cs` before LoadPlatformDescription) plus the
# storeback stubs for INTC / PORT / PWC / SYSREG / EFM / AOS / MSTP
# at the addresses the firmware writes during init. printers.test
# reaches the chip via creality-ender2pro-hc32 / anycubic-kobra-go-2022
# / anycubic-kobra-plus-2022 at config-parse depth; this is the
# firmware-boot regression target for the C# UART and storeback path.
# The PA3PA2 dict variant is used here (USART1 host link on
# PA3/PA2); the PA7PA8 variant routes through the same .repl + C#
# model so a separate test would not exercise additional infrastructure.
DICTIONARY hc32f460-serial-PA3PA2.dict
CONFIG hc32f460_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR hc32f460_smoke.fixture.json

# A few harmless gcode lines so klippy gets past klippy:ready.
M114
M105
M105
M105

# klippy connected and stayed connected long enough to do the
# clocksync handshake against the firmware's generic/armcm_timer view.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
